  "status_text": "Six families of graphs now carry a saving from NOT gates that grows with their size, each resting on its own checked rows: on one of the sharpest, a circuit without NOT gates needs exactly 2n - 1 AND/OR gates of fan-in two on one-a-side inputs and one with NOT gates at most 4, at every size from 2 [L-meta-20573, L-meta-20574, L-meta-20572]. All six savings are linear; whether any graph can be made more than 2n - 5 gates cheaper is the bet on the desk [L-meta-19158]. Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
